I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it as f96ae553. session_plan/ is gitignored, so it needed git add -f; the earlier assessment commits include the file too.

State: The harness verified the build and tests are green at HEAD. The last 4 evolve runs passed, with no reverts in 14 days.

Size-gate traps: Any task touching these two files can revert itself:
• src/context.rs is 2035 lines and not on the grandfathered list. 15 more lines makes cargo test fail.
• src/help.rs is 90 lines past its recorded size. 10 more lines makes it fail.

Reproduced with the built binary:
• #1154: yoyo config get with no key prints a usage line and exits 0. The usage line also uses the chat-window form /config get.
• #1155: yoyo lint unsafe, yoyo risk history and yoyo risk validate still tell shell users to type slash commands. These are the natural next pair, on the same code as #1127 and #1153.

Ticket actions taken this phase:
• #1149 is closed. @yuanhao answered at 09:42Z: keep -p and piped runs auto-approving tool calls, and keep that disclosed. The docs change already shipped on Day 252, so I commented and closed it.
• My own safety guard blocked me three times. These were two heredocs and one gh issue comment that only quoted test strings containing a delete-home-directory command. That's the class #1102 tracks. The message also misleads: it says the command "contains 'rm -rf /'" when it only contained the ~ form, because it prints the rule's name, not what it found. I recorded the first two hits on #1102 (the comment posting them was the third block) and noted the wording as a small fix candidate.

Research: I looked up the Claude Code releases from Nov 4 and 6, after my last saved scan. I saved the comparison to yopedia.
• New gap: Claude Code has a setting that denies any tool call that would have needed approval, and the run carries on. yoyo has no opt-in like that for unattended runs. Adding one as a setting or flag wouldn't change the default he just decided to keep. It's a new feature, so it would need a ticket first.
• Already covered: Claude Code fixed a permission bypass where VAR=value words in front of a command hid it from checks. Going by the existing tests (I didn't run them), yoyo's deny checks already handle that.
